      "text": "To determine the range of the function \\( G(x) = |x+1| - |x-1| \\), we need to analyze the behavior of the function by considering different cases based on the values of \\( x \\).\n\n### Step 1: Identify the critical points\nThe expressions inside the absolute values change sign at \\( x = -1 \\) and \\( x = 1 \\). Therefore, we will consider three intervals: \\( (-\\infty, -1) \\), \\( [-1, 1] \\), and \\( (1, \\infty) \\).\n\n### Step 2: Analyze each interval\n\n#### Case 1: \\( x < -1 \\)\nFor \\( x < -1 \\):\n\\[ |x+1| = -(x+1) = -x-1 \\]\n\\[ |x-1| = -(x-1) = -x+1 \\]\nThus,\n\\[ G(x) = (-x-1) - (-x+1) = -x-1 + x-1 = -2 \\]\nSo, for \\( x < -1 \\), \\( G(x) = -2 \\).\n\n#### Case 2: \\( -1 \\leq x \\leq 1 \\)\nFor \\( -1 \\leq x \\leq 1 \\):\n\\[ |x+1| = x+1 \\]\n\\[ |x-1| = -(x-1) = -x+1 \\]\nThus,\n\\[ G(x) = (x+1) - (-x+1) = x+1 + x-1 = 2x \\]\nSo, for \\( -1 \\leq x \\leq 1 \\), \\( G(x) = 2x \\).\n\n#### Case 3: \\( x > 1 \\)\nFor \\( x > 1 \\):\n\\[ |x+1| = x+1 \\]\n\\[ |x-1| = x-1 \\]\nThus,\n\\[ G(x) = (x+1) - (x-1) = x+1 - x+1 = 2 \\]\nSo, for \\( x > 1 \\), \\( G(x) = 2 \\).\n\n### Step 3: Combine the results\nFrom the analysis above, we have:\n- For \\( x < -1 \\), \\( G(x) = -2 \\)\n- For \\( -1 \\leq x \\leq 1 \\), \\( G(x) = 2x \\), which ranges from \\( -2 \\) to \\( 2 \\) (since \\( 2x \\) is continuous over this interval)\n- For \\( x > 1 \\), \\( G(x) = 2 \\)\n\nCombining these results, the function \\( G(x) \\) can take any value in the interval \\([-2, 2]\\).\n\n### Step 4: Conclusion\nThe range of the function \\( G(x) = |x+1| - |x-1| \\) is \\(\\boxed{[-2, 2]}\\).",
